  "id": "car",
  "term": "CAR",
  "definition": "CAR usually refers to chimeric antigen receptor T-cell therapy, a cancer treatment in which a person’s own T cells are genetically modified to recognize and attack cancer cells. It is used especially for some blood cancers when standard treatments have not worked, though it can cause serious immune-related and neurological side effects.",
